      "title": "Identity Vault: Troubleshooting Login Loops and Token Refresh Failures",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for resolving persistent login loops, unexpected logouts, and HTTP 401 errors caused by token refresh failures or federation issues in Identity Vault.",
      "content_body": "Login loops in Identity Vault often stem from expired certificates, identity provider outages, or misconfigured federation trust relationships. Begin by checking the status of the upstream identity provider and verifying that the service certificates have not expired. If the infrastructure is healthy, the issue may be operator error; review recent configuration changes to the federation settings. For immediate relief, perform a token/session reset for affected users. If the problem persists, engage the vendor to review the certificate chain and federation logs, and provide customer education on expected re-authentication behaviors during maintenance windows."
